          "type": "user",
          "text": "# Vercel AI SDK Overview\n\n## 1. Using with Anthropic/Claude Models\n\nThe AI SDK provides a unified interface for working with multiple LLM providers, including Anthropic. Rather than using the Anthropic SDK directly, you import from the AI SDK:\n\n```typescript\nimport { generateText } from \"ai\"\nimport { anthropic } from \"@ai-sdk/anthropic\"\n\nconst { text } = await generateText({\n  model: anthropic(\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"),\n  prompt: \"Your prompt here\"\n})\n```\n\n## 2. Handling Streaming Responses\n\nThe SDK abstracts away provider-specific streaming differences. Use `streamText` for streaming outputs:\n\n```typescript\nimport { streamText } from \"ai\"\n\nconst stream = await streamText({\n  model: anthropic(\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"),\n  prompt: \"Your prompt\"\n})\n```\n\nThis provides a consistent API regardless of whether you're using Claude, OpenAI, Google, or other supported providers.\n\n## 3. Tool Calls and Results\n\nThe AI SDK includes built-in support for tool calling. Define tools and let the SDK handle the orchestration automatically, managing the back-and-forth between model requests and tool execution.\n\n## 4. Key Differences from Anthropic SDK\n\nThe primary advantage is **standardization**: \"The AI SDK standardizes integrating artificial intelligence models across supported providers.\" This means identical code patterns work across different models and providers, reducing provider lock-in and simplifying multi-model deployments.\n\n## 5. Installation and Setup\n\nInstall via npm:\n```bash\nnpm install ai @ai-sdk/anthropic\n```\n\nSet your API key as an environment variable (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`), then import and use as shown above.\n\nThe framework-agnostic approach supports React, Next.js, Vue, Svelte, Node.js, and more.",
