          "type": "user",
          "text": "# Using generateText and streamText in AI SDK Core\n\n## generateText Function\n\n**Purpose**: Generates complete text responses for non-interactive use cases like email drafting or document summarization.\n\n**Basic Usage**:\n```javascript\nconst { text } = await generateText({\n  model: 'openai/gpt-4.1',\n  prompt: 'Write a vegetarian lasagna recipe for 4 people.',\n});\n```\n\n**Key Parameters**:\n- `model`: The LLM to use\n- `prompt`: Your text request\n- `system`: Optional instructions defining behavior (e.g., \"You are a professional writer\")\n- `maxTokens`: Limit response length\n- `tools`: Define available functions for the model to call\n\n**Return Values**:\nThe result object provides access to `text`, `toolCalls`, `usage`, `finishReason`, and `response` properties containing metadata and generated content.\n\n## streamText Function\n\n**Purpose**: Streams text progressively, ideal for interactive applications where immediate feedback matters.\n\n**Basic Usage**:\n```javascript\nconst result = streamText({\n  model: 'openai/gpt-4.1',\n  prompt: 'Invent a new holiday and describe its traditions.',\n});\n\nfor await (const textPart of result.textStream) {\n  console.log(textPart);\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- `result.textStream` works as both a `ReadableStream` and `AsyncIterable`\n- Uses backpressure—tokens generate only when consumed\n- `onError` callback captures errors without crashing servers\n- `onFinish` callback triggers upon completion with final metrics\n\n**Callbacks Available**:\n- `onChunk`: Processes individual stream events (text, tool-calls, reasoning)\n- `onFinish`: Executes when streaming completes with aggregated data\n\nBoth functions support tool integration and structured outputs for advanced LLM capabilities.",
