          "text": "# Tool Calling with AI SDK: A Comprehensive Guide\n\n## 1. Defining Tools\n\nTools are created using the `tool()` helper function with three key components:\n\n- **Description**: Explains what the tool does to influence model selection\n- **inputSchema**: A Zod schema defining parameters that the LLM consumes and validates\n- **execute**: An optional async function processing inputs and returning results\n\n```typescript\nconst weatherTool = tool({\n  description: 'Get the weather in a location',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    location: z.string().describe('The location to get the weather for'),\n  }),\n  execute: async ({ location }) => ({\n    location,\n    temperature: 72 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 21) - 10,\n  }),\n});\n```\n\n## 2. Tool Execution: Automatic vs Manual\n\nBy default, tools execute automatically when called by the model. However, you can skip execution by omitting the `execute` function to forward calls elsewhere (client, queue, etc.).\n\nTools receive execution context as a second parameter:\n- **toolCallId**: Identifier for tracking\n- **messages**: Full conversation history\n- **abortSignal**: Cancellation token\n- **experimental_context**: Arbitrary context passed from parent call\n\n## 3. Getting Tool Results\n\nAccess results via the `response.messages` property, which contains \"all the text, tool calls, tool results\" \nfrom generation. Add these to conversation history for multi-turn interactions.\n\nFor streaming, use `onFinish` callbacks or `steps` property to access intermediate results from each generation step.\n\n## 4. Multi-Step Control: stopWhen Parameter\n\nUse `stopWhen` to enable agentic loops. The model generates text after tool execution, potentially using multiple tools sequentially. Common condition: `stepCountIs(5)` limits to 5 maximum steps.\n\nThe `stopWhen` conditions evaluate only \"when the last step contains tool results.\"\n\n## 5. Manual Tool Call Handling\n\nFor custom workflows, implement the `onStepFinish` callback triggered when \"all text deltas, tool calls, and tool results for the step are available.\"\n\nAccess intermediate calls via `steps.flatMap(step => step.toolCalls)` to inspect and process results before deciding whether to continue generation or handle tool calls yourself.",
